- Some countries only require 3 months of validity beyond the stay, and a few require validity only for the duration of stay — it varies. Always check the destination country’s embassy/consulate website or the visa guidance where you’re applying.
- If your passport expiry is too close, the usual fix is to renew your passport before applying. Most consulates allow you to apply for a visa once you have the renewed passport.

What I can do next
- If you tell me which expiry date you meant and the destination country (or paste just the expiry date, not your SSN), I’ll tell you whether that looks too close for a typical six-month visa and point to the specific rule or embassy page if you want.

