First — a quick privacy note: Social Security numbers are extremely sensitive. I won’t store or repeat the full number you posted; if we need to reference it, I’ll only use the last four digits.

A couple quick points and then a question so I can give precise advice:

- Social Security numbers themselves don’t “expire.” So the SSN isn’t what determines whether a visa can be issued or used.
- I think when you say “expiry date” you mean a document like your passport (or possibly a driver’s license or the visa itself). Which one do you mean?

General guidance about “six-month” rules (what consulates/airlines commonly require)
- Many countries require your passport be valid for at least six months beyond your intended date of entry OR beyond the end date of your planned stay. That means:
  - If you plan to enter on July 1 and stay for up to six months, your passport should typically be valid until at least January 1 (and in many cases six months after that entry or departure date—check the exact rule for the destination).
- If your passport expires sooner than that, you should renew it before applying for the visa or before travel — airlines can refuse boarding and border officials can deny entry.
- If the visa itself would expire before the passport expiry, that can also be a problem because visas are usually linked to a valid passport. If your passport will expire while the visa is still valid, it’s safer to renew the passport first (or carry both old and new passports if the visa is in the old one; check embassy guidance).

What I can do next
- If you tell me which country’s visa you’re applying for and the exact expiry date you’re worried about (passport expiry or visa expiry and the date), I’ll check the typical requirement and tell you whether that expiry is “too close” and whether you should renew before applying.
- If you want help filling the form, I can also suggest wording or show how to enter only the last four digits where appropriate and how to verify the form’s security before submitting sensitive info.

Which expiry date do you mean, and what country/visa type is this for?

