- Confirm which document the form means by “expiry date” (passport? ID?).
- Check the destination country’s official consulate/embassy or immigration website for passport validity requirements.
- If you tell me the country you’re applying to and your intended travel dates (or date of entry), I can look up the specific requirement and tell you whether your passport expiry is a problem.
- If the form genuinely needs your SSN, enter the full SSN only on the secure form — never send it over insecure channels or public chat.

If you’d like, tell me:
- the country for the visa and
- your intended travel/entry date (or your passport expiry date),
and I’ll check whether the expiry is too close for a six-month visa.

