Response (FULL, NOT TRUNCATED):
Quick privacy note: I can't store or process full Social Security numbers. It's safer to give only the last four digits when needed — you already included those, which is fine. Please avoid posting the full SSN in public or insecure places.

A couple of quick clarifying questions before I advise:
- When the form asks for an "expiry date," do you mean your passport expiry, your SSN card/authorization expiry, or something else?
- Which country's visa are you applying for (or where will you use the visa)?

General guidance you can use right away
- SSNs themselves generally do not “expire.” If the form is asking for an SSN expiry, it’s likely actually asking about a different document (usually a passport or a work/immigration authorization card). Check the form instructions.
- For a six-month visa, most countries require your passport to be valid for at least six months beyond your intended date of departure (or beyond the end of your intended stay). If your passport expires within six months of the end of your trip, that is usually “too close” and you should renew before travelling.
- Some countries only require 3 months of validity; some have different rules. Always confirm with the specific consulate/immigration website for the country you’ll visit.

Example calculation
- If your trip starts May 10 and the visa allows a six-month stay, the visa end date would be around November 10. Many consulates would want your passport valid at least through May 10 + 6 months (i.e., at least through November 10) and commonly prefer an additional safety buffer so they require validity for six months beyond your planned departure. If your passport expires before that, renew it.

What I can do for you
- If you tell me which expiry date the form is asking for (passport or other) and the passport expiry date (just the date, not your SSN), plus your planned travel dates or visa start date, I can quickly tell you whether the expiration looks too close.
- I can also point you to the specific consulate requirement if you tell me the destination country.

Would you like to share the expiry date and your travel/visa start date (no SSN needed) so I can check?

